  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "transport",
      "title": "Server-side change notification",
      "items": [
        "The engine commits changes to assigned declarations and persistent change records. The notifier enqueues the current tokens with a generation-specific deduplication key.",
        "A configured pusher prompts the device to poll. The device receives the command in the MDM server response, then follows token comparison and manifest synchronization."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "transport",
      "title": "Device synchronization",
      "items": [
        "The command Data carries TokensResponse. The device compares DeclarationsToken with its stored token: unchanged state ends synchronization; changed state leads to declaration-items and needed declaration fetches.",
        "A tokens check-in is the fallback for a command without Data, not an unconditional extra request. This server carries the Endpoint value inside DeclarativeManagement check-in to /mdm; status reports are separate."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "storage",
      "title": "State preservation",
      "items": [
        "Ordinary enrollment reset or checkout clears declarative state through the service hook. Controlled profile replacement avoids that reset."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "transport",
